<figure class="fig-tight">
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 340 120" role="img" aria-label="Fig P05.1 — the surds on the root-2 number line: three dots on whole multiples of the standard surd, their sum 4√2 marked in red">
<line x1="20" y1="72" x2="316" y2="72" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<polygon points="316,67.5 326,72 316,76.5" fill="#555f6e"/>
<line x1="25" y1="69" x2="25" y2="75" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="25" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">0</text>
<line x1="83" y1="69" x2="83" y2="75" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="83" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">√2</text>
<line x1="141" y1="69" x2="141" y2="75" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="141" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">2√2</text>
<line x1="199" y1="69" x2="199" y2="75" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="199" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">3√2</text>
<line x1="257" y1="69" x2="257" y2="75" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="257" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">4√2</text>
<line x1="315" y1="69" x2="315" y2="75" stroke="#555f6e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="315" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">5√2</text>
<circle cx="141" cy="72" r="4" fill="#3574d4"/>
<text x="141" y="56" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3574d4">√8</text>
<circle cx="199" cy="72" r="4" fill="#3574d4"/>
<text x="199" y="56" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3574d4">√18</text>
<circle cx="315" cy="72" r="4" fill="#3574d4"/>
<text x="315" y="56" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3574d4">√50</text>
<circle cx="257" cy="72" r="4" fill="#c25b4a"/>
<text x="257" y="56" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c25b4a">4√2</text>
<text x="170" y="112" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">the three surds sit on whole multiples of √2; the sum (red) does too</text>
</svg>
<figcaption><strong>Fig P05.1.</strong> The three surds land on the √2-number line: √8 = 2√2, √18 = 3√2 and √50 = 5√2 sit exactly on whole multiples of the standard surd √2 — and so does their sum (red): \((5 - 3 + 2)\sqrt{2} = 4\sqrt{2}\), certified by the exact square check \((\sqrt{50} - \sqrt{18} + \sqrt{8})^2 = 32 = (4\sqrt{2})^2\). Every tick and dot position machine-verified in this pass's lab.</figcaption>
</figure>
